In article <1nbjgf$2fg@terminator.rs.itd.umich.edu> pbotts@cedar.cic.net (Paul Botts) writes:
>Got a couple of questions for the wizards out there. No hints please, I
>wanna be spoiled till I scream.
>1) How do I proceed down from the castle level?

     I'll defer this to someone who's actually seen the castle level. :)

>2) My friend without net access is very unhappy with me, because he got
>his first wish for his neutral priest, and I suggested Excaliber. He
>wished for it, got it, but got somewarning message, and when he tried to
>wield it, he died! Oops....so what happened? I know only lawful characters
>can do the fountain trick with a longsword, but are non-lawful characters
>now forbidden to wield lawful artifacts?

     In 3.1, all aligned weapons (be they lawful, neutral, or chaotic) do 
damage to characters of other alignments who try to wield them.  Excalibur is
a lawful weapon, so neutrals and chaotics get zapped by it.  I believe that
Vorpal Blade is a good weapon for neutrals to wish for, and of course there's
always Stormy for chaotics. :)

>3) He had already tried to wish for Mjollnir, and got a message that "That
>does not exist in this dungeon." What does that mean? I think his wording
>was right on the wish.

     I believe that Mjolnir has only one l.  Yes, Nethack penalizes spelling
mistakes. :)

     As long as I need to come up with a few more lines before I can post this,
let me echo the sentiments of some others on the net that wands of sleep are
more than a bit unfair to the player right now.  When I zap a monster with one,
I usually get in no more than three or four hits before the monster wakes up.
Yet, I just had a barbarian with 114 hit points, a -6 AC and a ring of
regeneration get taken from full hit points all the way down to zero and death
after getting cornered by three orcs and zapped with one of these.  They're
wands of death on the installment plan... :(
